takes AI. Ensuring that an experiment or a system deployment can be perfectly reconstructed via hashes allows for higher intellectual merit in validation studies. It solves a real-world tension between data minimization (privacy) and regulatory traceability (compliance), which has broader impact on how secure AI pipelines are designed.\n\n    *   The proposal is technically sound, directly addresses the legal requirement for high-risk biometric systems, and uses best practices (content-addressing) to ensure the integrity of the data used in those systems. From an R&D perspective, this infrastructure allows for precise auditing and reproduction of system behavior, which is essential for scientific rigor in AI development.\n\n    *   Rationale: The use of content-addressed snapshots provides a rigorous technical foundation for provenance and reproducibility in biometric pipelines, effectively balancing regulatory compliance with data minimization.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 90 (It's a very practical, well-defined solution to a mandatory requirement that enables scientific auditing).",
