ic recording of events, timestamps, input data, etc., in a systematic way.\n\n    *   The proposal reduces friction for researchers by automating regulatory compliance.\n    *   It ensures consistency in logging across various prototypes, which is scientifically valuable for debugging and auditing.\n    *   It transforms a repetitive engineering burden into a one-time architectural investment.\n\n    *   Rationale: This removes the repetitive overhead of manual instrumentation from the research process, allowing researchers to focus on model innovation while ensuring standardized, high-quality data for traceability and auditability across all prototypes.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: High (e.g., 90+). It's a pragmatic engineering solution that protects research velocity without sacrificing compliance.",
