nts/weights) and Compliance (technical files).\n\n    *   The proposal specifically targets the requirements mentioned in Recital 71 regarding technical documentation.\n    *   It introduces an enforcement mechanism (diff-checks) to prevent the \"stale document\" problem common in fast-paced AI R&D.\n    *   This is critical for survival and compliance.\n\n    *   Rationale: The proposal directly implements the mandate of Recital 71 to keep technical documentation up to date throughout the system's lifetime, using automated checks to ensure alignment between actual model changes and recorded evidence. This significantly reduces the risk of non-compliance during audits or post-market monitoring.\n    *   Decision: approve.\n    *   Promise: 95 (Extremely high; it solves a core compliance pain point with a concrete operational strategy).",
