y implemented.\nSome changes, or reasonably feasible measures =3. Requires coordination with two partner institutions, standardise schema, release logs under open licence, host semi-annual challenge. That's significant change, expensive/difficult? Could be significant change, expensive or difficult but not totally impossible =2. Hmm.\n\nImplementing open benchmark requires legal review, anonymisation, infrastructure. Significant change. Might be 2 = significant change, or expensive or difficult, but not totally impossible.\n\nLet's decide scores:\nparadigm_relatedness: evidence sentence then score.\noriginality\napplicability\neffectiveness\nacceptability\nimplementability\n\nI think:\nparadigm_relatedness 3 (paradigm stretching)\noriginality 3\napplicability 4? Let's pick 4 solves identified problem directly related.\neffectiveness 3\nacceptability 2 (offends sensibilities somewhat due to biometric data sharing)\nimplementability 2\n\nProvide one sentence evidence each.\n\nNeed format: <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Probably output list.\n\nReturn rating echoing id exactly.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid P1243\nparadigm_relatedness_evidence: ...\nparadigm_relatedness: 3\n\netc.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nMake sure each evidence is one sentence.\n\nProceed.",
