p between lab's R&D and its compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners...)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working unchanged\n\nThis is a review gate. Introduces process element but still treats compliance as logging practice. Slightly paradigm stretching? It converts abstract duty into engineering acceptance test. Might be slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements but still treats compliance as logging practice. Could be 2. Or maybe 1 paradigm preserving? Standard compliance gate is common. I'd say 2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice.\n\noriginality: degree rare but ingenious... 4 not expressed before AND ingenious... 3 unusual interesting shows some imagination. 2 interesting. 1 common mundane boring. Compliance-by-design review gate is common mundane. Probably 1 = common, mundane, boring. Or 2 interesting? Might be common. I'll give 1.\n\nNeed one sentence evidence each then score.\n\nOutput format: echo id exactly. For each subscale give <subscale>_evidence then <subscale>. Order listed: acceptability, implementability, effectiveness, applicability, paradigm_relatedness, originality.\n\nProbably JSON? It says return rating echoing its id exactly. Might produce lines.\n\nI'll output:\n\nid: P1668\nacceptability_evidence: ...\nacceptability: 4\netc.\n\nEnsure one sentence evidence.\n\nLet's craft sentences.\n\nacceptability_evidence: The gate enforces existing legal logging duties without violating norms or business practice and is a standard compliance control. -> score 4\n\nimplementability_evidence: It requires adding a sign-off template and q